# Order-block data collection — crontab example (IST). Adjust paths.
# The options archive only grows on days the recorder runs: Kite does not serve
# expired option history, so a missed session is lost for good.
#
#   crontab -e   then paste with your paths:
#
# m  h   dom mon dow  command
  50 7   *   *   1-5  cd ~/nse-cli && .venv/bin/python model_cli.py kite-master      >> logs/ob.log 2>&1
# 09:10 — one of these two (ob-paper records everything ob-record does):
  10 9   *   *   1-5  cd ~/nse-cli && .venv/bin/python model_cli.py ob-paper        >> logs/ob.log 2>&1
# 10 9   *   *   1-5  cd ~/nse-cli && .venv/bin/python model_cli.py ob-record       >> logs/ob.log 2>&1
  25 15  *   *   1-5  cd ~/nse-cli && .venv/bin/python model_cli.py archive-chain --expiries 2 >> logs/ob.log 2>&1
  0  16  *   *   1-5  cd ~/nse-cli && .venv/bin/python model_cli.py ob-backfill --days 3 --options >> logs/ob.log 2>&1
  10 16  *   *   1-5  cd ~/nse-cli && .venv/bin/python model_cli.py ob-coverage --days 1 >> logs/ob.log 2>&1
#
# The Kite session must be refreshed each morning (`model_cli.py kite-login`);
# it expires at 06:00 IST and every job above fails loudly without it.
